id: pm-bnrndo
title: Terminal release transitions retain stale claim_principal ownership
description: "CodeRabbit PR #753 found that closed items remain durably owned after pm release because terminal projections retain claim_principal. Fix release semantics so both assignee and claim principal clear through append-only PM history, add regression coverage, and repair the affected PR items through the CLI."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-26T20:29:07.269Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-26T20:55:29.768Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-26T20:55:26.628Z"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: pm release clears assignee and claim_principal for terminal and active items through a recorded history transition; affected PR #753 items have no stale ownership; regression tests prove projection and history behavior
parent: pm-dj98
resolution: Release transitions now clear terminal claim principals through append-only history.
expected_result: "Releasing any claimed item clears both assignee and claim_principal, including after close removed assignee."
actual_result: Unit regression and live repairs prove terminal releases append ownership cleanup and leave no durable claim principal.
