comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-26T20:29:07.269Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-07-26: searched every status for closed claim_principal release ownership, release clears claim principal, and stale terminal ownership. Existing claim atomicity items pm-8t5x and pm-z8qd4k cover acquisition identity, while PR items only exhibit the symptom; no item owns release-side durable ownership cleanup, so this is the canonical review-found lifecycle defect."
  "2026-07-26T20:35:34.178Z","harness:codex","Review implementation: runRelease now treats an orphaned claim_principal as durable ownership that requires a recorded release transition even when a terminal close already removed assignee. The rebuilt globally installed CLI successfully repaired closed pm-i7indd without force; the remaining actively reopened PR items will prove cleanup on their normal close/release path."
  "2026-07-26T20:53:21.286Z","harness:codex","Final local verification: repo-wide coverage passed 375 test files and 6,428 tests at exact 100% statements (44,307/44,307), branches (31,445/31,445), functions (9,061/9,061), and lines (43,046/43,046). Full lint passed ESLint, zero jscpd clones, static quality, 100% docstrings, package boundary, token budgets, SDK surface, import-cost, and transport-floor gates. Security scan and pnpm audit reported no secrets or vulnerabilities; packed npx acceptance passed all 15 bundled packages."
  "2026-07-26T20:55:21.435Z","harness:codex","Acceptance evidence: linked claim lifecycle test passed 24/24 through pm test in an isolated schema tracker. Live repaired pm-i7indd already has no claim_principal; the five reopened review items will exercise the same close-then-release path."
